; The questions about the regulated workflow (§16), kept beside the model.

; Can a case get stuck — reachable, but never settleable? `live` asks whether a
; settled docket is still reachable from EVERY reachable situation. Even where
; the assignee slot is empty (the escalation state), the case can still be
; assigned and then settled, so the guarantee holds: no reachable case is ever
; stranded.
(property settle-able
  "the case can always still be settled"
  (live (is claim-1.stage settled)))

; May the assignee slot be empty here — and must it always be fillable? The slot
; is vacatable and starts empty; `live (defined …)` confirms it can always be
; (re)filled from any reachable situation.
(property assignee-fillable
  "the assignee slot can always still be filled"
  (live (defined claim-1.assignee)))

; Which reassignment moves can break the unit-of-record law? `pol check` reports
; officer-in-unit can be broken by reassign-to-fraud and reassign-to-kyc (both
; write case.officer, an arrow the law's route traverses). We acknowledge both,
; recording ownership (§16.3). settle / assign / escalate touch none of the
; law's arrows, so accepting them would be reported `stale`.
(accept reassign-to-fraud officer-in-unit)
(accept reassign-to-kyc   officer-in-unit)
